Enhancement: Add reusable release workflow for ownCloud Classic apps

A tag push on an app repository now builds, signs and publishes the app tarball
as a GitHub Release. Signing is delegated to ocsign instead of
`occ integrity:sign-app`, so no bootstrapped ownCloud server is needed - which
is why app Makefiles previously skipped signing silently in CI. The workflow
asserts that every published tarball carries a valid schema v2
`appinfo/signature.json`, turning that silent skip into a hard failure.

https://github.com/owncloud/reusable-workflows/pull/87
